WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.576
Inferact plans an

00:00:01.388 --> 00:00:02.531
autonomous inference

00:00:02.343 --> 00:00:03.569
system built around

00:00:03.381 --> 00:00:04.241
vLLM

00:00:04.782 --> 00:00:06.515
vLLM co-creator Simon

00:00:06.327 --> 00:00:07.364
Mo explains that

00:00:07.176 --> 00:00:08.425
Inferact is building

00:00:08.237 --> 00:00:09.227
a system that

00:00:09.039 --> 00:00:10.265
tunes vLLM for

00:00:10.077 --> 00:00:10.949
new models

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:12.376
chips and workloads

00:00:12.188 --> 00:00:12.918
on its own

00:00:13.131 --> 00:00:14.499
while vLLM stays

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:15.572
open and engine

00:00:15.383 --> 00:00:16.586
improvements go back

00:00:16.398 --> 00:00:17.199
upstream

00:00:17.734 --> 00:00:18.453
In an X

00:00:18.265 --> 00:00:18.984
article

00:00:19.078 --> 00:00:20.269
Building an Autonomous

00:00:20.081 --> 00:00:21.106
Inference System

00:00:21.366 --> 00:00:22.403
Mo argues that

00:00:22.215 --> 00:00:23.193
the model ×

00:00:23.005 --> 00:00:24.361
hardware × workload

00:00:24.173 --> 00:00:25.210
space can't be

00:00:25.022 --> 00:00:26.224
tuned by hand

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:27.728
Many people have

00:00:27.564 --> 00:00:28.801
asked what inferact

00:00:28.613 --> 00:00:29.674
is building and

00:00:29.604 --> 00:00:30.346
what it means

00:00:30.158 --> 00:00:31.242
for vllmproject

00:00:31.758 --> 00:00:32.772
Full story on

00:00:32.583 --> 00:00:33.479
the dashboard
